          "title": "You'll want to know: مسافت",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مسافت — masāfat — \"a distance travelled; a long way\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پہاڑوں تک کی مسافت لمبی ہے۔ pahāṛoṅ tak kī masāfat lambī hai. It is a long way to the mountains."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مسافت (masāfat) is usually traced, through Persian, to Arabic masāfa, \"a distance\"; it is a cousin of مسافر and سفر."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
