          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تھکانا — thakānā — \"to tire (someone) out\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "لمبے سفر نے سارا کو تھکا دیا۔ lambe safar ne sārā ko thakā diyā. The long journey wore Sara out."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with نے (he or she …): اس نے گھوڑے کو تھکایا, us ne ghoṛe ko thakāyā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تھکانا (thakānā) is built on تھکنا, \"to get tired\", which comes from sthakk, \"stop, halt\", a form CDIAL reconstructs (CDIAL 13737): this is the form for tiring someone else."
            }
          ]
        },
